{"topic": "TCP/IP Model", "part": {"part": 1, "title": "Four TCP/IP layers and IP addressing/routing", "duration_target": 45, "script": "The TCP/IP suite is organized into four layers: Link, Internet, Transport and Application, from bottom to top. Each host has a unique IP address. Routers read these addresses and forward packets toward their destination using routing tables. Thus, IP addressing uniquely identifies each host, and routing tables in routers determine the next hop for each destination, enabling best\u2011effort delivery across the Internet.", "visual_plan": ["Show TCP/IP layers stack", "Display hosts with IPs, router and routing table", "Summarize IP role"], "scenes": [{"scene_id": "s1", "narration": "The TCP/IP suite is organized into four layers: Link, Internet, Transport and Application, from bottom to top.", "clear": false, "elements": [{"id": "title", "type": "TEXT", "animation": "WRITE", "x": 50.0, "y": 8.0, "w": null, "h": null, "text": "TCP/IP Model", "label": "", "size": "title", "color": "ink", "from_id": "", "to_id": "", "x2": null, "y2": null, "steps": [], "direction": "horizontal", "rows": [], "nodes": [], "edges": [], "target": "", "page": null, "to_x": null, "to_y": null}, {"id": "layers", "type": "FLOW", "animation": "SEQUENTIAL_REVEAL", "x": 50.0, "y": 30.0, "w": 30.0, "h": 40.0, "text": "", "label": "", "size": "normal", "color": "", "from_id": "", "to_id": "", "x2": null, "y2": null, "steps": ["Link", "Internet", "Transport", "Application"], "direction": "vertical", "rows": [], "nodes": [], "edges": [], "target": "", "page": null, "to_x": null, "to_y": null}]}, {"scene_id": "s2", "narration": "Each host has a unique IP address. Routers read these addresses and forward packets toward their destination using routing tables.", "clear": true, "elements": [{"id": "hostA", "type": "BOX", "animation": "DRAW", "x": 20.0, "y": 70.0, "w": 20.0, "h": 12.0, "text": "", "label": "Host A", "size": "normal", "color": "blue", "from_id": "", "to_id":